{"availability":"available","full":"winwiz1/crisp-react","name":"crisp-react","description":"React boilerplate written in TypeScript with a variety of Jamstack and full stack deployments. Comes with SSR and without need to learn a framework. Helps to split a monolithic React app into multiple SPAs and avoid vendor lock-in.","category":"Education","language":"TypeScript","stars":190,"forks":28,"created":"2019-08-08T03:03:45Z","updated":"2023-03-14T19:57:43Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://crisp-react.winwiz1.com","topics":["boilerplate","cloudflare","cloudflare-pages","containerization","docker","express","frontend","fullstack","jamstack","nodejs","prerender","react","ssr","static-site-generator","typescript","webapp","webpack"],"demo":"https://crisp-react.winwiz1.com/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T19:06:52.126Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T19:06:52.126Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T19:06:52.126Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T19:06:52.126Z","stars":190,"forks":28}],"technologies":["React","Node.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Crisp React can optionally split a monolithic React app into multiple Single Page Applications (SPAs) and selectively prerender the landing/index page of any SPA at the build time. This innovative flexibility can offer the best performance for many websites, more about it later. Yet it doesn't come at the price of complicating the solution which remains as simple as a React application could possibly be.","For example, the Router is arguably one of the most important SPA components because it drives the application by controlling its page switching. Crisp React doesn't use a custom Router, in each SPA the routing is managed by a separate instance of React Router which is the de facto standard for React SPAs.","The value offered by Crisp React is not limited to performance. On the one hand, the value comes from what this solution doesn't bring about. There is no need to learn a framework, depend on it and use non-portable programming constructs in the React components you write, therefore no vendor lock-in. On the other hand, the list of useful features includes:"],"features":["The optional splitting of a React application into multiple SPAs (each rendered by its own bundle) improves the application loading time. The vendor bundle contains nodemodules/ dependencies and is reused between SPAs…","Every SPA has a landing page displayed during initial rendering by the component included into the SPA. In webpack terminology such a component is called entry point. An SPA (and its bundle) is comprised of this…","Each SPA is defined using 4 pieces of data: name, entry point (e.g. the landing page component) and two boolean flags. Ignore the flags for a moment. There is also an appTitle, it provides the application-wide default…","SPA's name \"first\" is used to define the SPA's landing page e.g. /first.html and name the bundle that renders the SPA: first.js. More information about all the configuration data pieces is provided in the configuration…","and then follow the instructions provided in the configuration file comments."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/winwiz1/crisp-react/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"5e8e4b790d2a9ad4095aebb768989c4a877b3d8c364493451ec56f1dd13de0c8","extractedAt":"2026-10-05T19:06:52.228Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T19:06:52.228Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Crisp React can optionally split a monolithic React app into multiple Single Page Applications (SPAs) and selectively prerender the landing/index page of any SPA at the build time. This innovative flexibility can offer the best performance for many websites, more about it later. Yet it doesn't come at the price of complicating the solution which remains as simple as a React application could possibly be.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/winwiz1/crisp-react/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"For example, one SPA can offer an introductory set of screens for the first-time user or handle login.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/winwiz1/crisp-react/blob/master/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"For example, you can have a Login SPA, Main SPA, Reporting SPA, Audit SPA, Admin SPA, etc.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/winwiz1/crisp-react/blob/master/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"5e8e4b790d2a9ad4095aebb768989c4a877b3d8c364493451ec56f1dd13de0c8","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/winwiz1/crisp-react/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T19:06:52.229Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2023-03-14T19:57:43Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/winwiz1/crisp-react/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T19:06:52.233Z","hash":"5e8e4b790d2a9ad4095aebb768989c4a877b3d8c364493451ec56f1dd13de0c8","originalBytes":67944,"storedBytes":67944,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["spa","cloudflare","build","page","name","react","configuration","cloud","client","heroku","one","domain","code","css","pages","stack","create","docker","full","google","jamstack","used","backend","repository","using","cdn","deployment","docs","app","free","add","data","each","e.g.","following","api","block","deployments","scenarios","section","seo","there","website","example","files","under","component","container","dns","project","provided","usage","which","available","ensure","less","login","option","two","after","both","crisp","deploy","new","solution","added","any","application","created","custom","file","indexed","other","script","set","start","steps","subdomain","crisp-react","demo","gcloud","record","rule","run","should","time","type","url","yarn","address","another","approach","builds","bundle","end","performance","production","service","single","spas","static","test","worker","access","browser","click","clone","command","compute","instance","only","same","ssr","would","case","class","coul